<markdown>

As part of GSoC, I am working on improving Rust support for obscure architectures, such as DEC Alpha, m68k, or SuperH.

In this article, I will document that process. I will go over all the steps required to compile Rust code for DEC Alpha using GCC. Compiler changes, library support, building GCC from source, and so on. 

Hopefully, this helps other people add Rust support for GCC-only architectures in the future. 

So, if you like hearing about weird architectures, join me on this ride :).

# Getting a cross-compiler

`rustc_codegen_gcc` is a Rust compiler backend(plugin) allowing us to use GCC to compile Rust code. Internally, it uses a library called `libgccjit` to comunictate with GCC.


</markdown>